097 mtp-draft-split-argmax: frozen-KV MTP draft head scores each rank's vocabulary share (topk == 1)

The Gemma 4 assistant draft keeps a full tied head (262144 x 1024 bf16 = 0.54 GB) and, with
skip_all_gather, every TP rank reads all of it at every draft step, then the worker runs a softmax
over the vocabulary to take one token. SGLANG_MTP_DRAFT_SPLIT_ARGMAX=1: each rank scores
vocab / tp_size rows, the ranks exchange (max logit, index as three base-256 digits) through one
bf16 all-reduce, and the logits handed to the worker are 0 with a 1 at the exact argmax; the worker
takes the argmax of the logits instead of softmax + max when topk == 1 (the score is unused in a
greedy chain). Ties resolve to the lowest token id as torch.max does. Target verification is
untouched, so outputs keep the target's distribution.
gemma4-31b TP=2, two interleaved boots per arm, spec cycle 24.17 / 24.20 -> 22.40 / 22.41 ms at
32K and 30.64 / 30.66 -> 28.87 / 28.89 ms at 131K; natural-prompt decode 202 -> 219 / 189 -> 204 /
128 -> 136 tok/s at 1K / 32K / 131K; greedy text identical on 5 prompts in all four boots.
Default (unset or 0) keeps upstream behaviour.
---
